{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle","id":1509497,"title":"Redeemed Tremere (What if the Tremere had remained in the Pentacle?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-24T10:53:04-07:00","id":1509497,"title":"Redeemed Tremere (What if the Tremere had remained in the Pentacle?)","content":"Hi everyone!<br /> <br /> Having read <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/tome-of-the-pentacle-tremere/\" target=\"_blank\">the most recent post about the Tremere in the Tome of the Pentacle</a>, I was struck by the question &quot;What if the Tremere had remained in the Pentacle?&quot; Would there be a way to capture the general vibe of the Tremere, as outlined in the above post, but also removing their soul sucking providence? After a bit of drafting, I think I've managed to get a good Order style write up for a redeemed Tremere.<br /> <br /> Please let me know what you think! Do you dig it? Do they have a distinct enough identity from the rest of the Orders? Would you want to play as them? I think I'll wait until TotP is out before I try and write up an Order merit at least!<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading! <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><u><b><b>The Tremere</b></b></u></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i>Magic Demands Conquest</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Don\u2019t come here just because you liked me pissing off the Hierarch. Yes, he can be a stubborn old coot, but I knew him when he was the rising star of the Ladder. Can you believe he was accused of being both a Guardian plant </i>and <i>a secret Libertine? I keep at him so he has to remember those days, remember what it was like to shake things up.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s what\u2019s important, memory. We all once were Sleepers, ignorant to the Lie around us and unable to do anything. After Awakening too many forget that fact, in the Diamond and out. The Tremere don\u2019t forget, even if the memories are painful. Instead, fight for the dreams you had when you were Asleep, fight for the dreams you had when you first Awoke and when you\u2019ve reached further than you could have imagined, go beyond that.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hierarch hasn\u2019t forgotten how to sulk like a teenager, so we\u2019re not going to wait. That verge needs mapping and whatever\u2019s been eating ghosts in there needs its ass kicked. Want to make some new memories?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The path to enlightenment is a blazing trail which others can follow. The Watchtowers are merely the first step on the path to Ascension, of unleashing the infinite power of the Awakened soul to conquer Truth and dethrone the Exarchs. The Fallen World is in shackles, but these chains reflect the Tyrants\u2019 fetters on the Supernal, a hierarchy of control by autocratic sub-souls and mystic satraps who believe themselves unassailable, the populace appeased with meaningless victories and easy pleasures within their designated realms. The Tremere defy this, assailing Mysteries and cracking open the walls of heaven, so that Truth will pour out unimpeded like blood from a wound. Like Prometheus, the Tremere fight the gods to steal Divine Fire so all the world can feel its warmth. They are dedicated iconoclasts, reformers and devil\u2019s advocates, often the loyal opposition within the Diamond rather than its leaders. The Tremere know the dangers of unchallenged authority better than any Order and will fight to keep the Awakened nation vital and strong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mages join the Tremere when they</b> want to seek challenge and danger, share Truth with others, challenge the structures they support, atone through acts of valour, or hunt monsters and Reapers who threaten the souls of Humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b>Core Beliefs: Shaking the Boundaries</b></b></span><br /> <br /> The origin of modern Tremere philosophy is derived from a sacred text, the Pure Suspire written by the Seven Martyrs, the founders of the renewed order who gave their lives to purge it of sin. It is derived from the original secretive text of the first Tremere order, who\u2019s opening treaties on struggle and enlightenment hid the literal soul devouring practised by its leadership. Not only is the new text purged of the prideful nihilism of its predecessor, it is freely available to any Mage who wishes to read it so that the virtue of the new Order can be seen by all. From the Pure Suspire and nine hundred years of internal debate, several tenets have coalesced by general consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b>Break the Gods</b></b></span><br /> <br /> The Awakened soul possesses limitless potential, but it is hemmed in on all sides by the hierarchy of the Exarchs. Supernal gaolers leer down at the Fallen World like gargoyles, wielding power they have not earned. Agents of the Tyrants seek to conceal and destroy what Mysteries they cannot hoard for themselves. Those with the strength to do so must bind and defeat these foes, smashing apart these pantheons of oppression and claim the secrets they guard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Scatter Their Thrones</span></b></b><br /> <br /> It is not enough to claim the Mysteries; strength must be mediated by righteousness and benevolence. Supernal Truths should be distributed to all those who need them, so they can never again be used as leverage against the ignorant. This does not advocate for Sleepers to have unfettered access, the Tremere respect the threat of Paradox, but the proliferation of any revealed knowledge is seen as a virtue. The majority of Temere preach the belief that every successful Awakening makes subsequent ones more likely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b>Protect All Souls</b></b></span><br /> <br /> Within all souls, from the deepest Sleeper to the grandest Archmaster, is power to change the world, if it can be unleashed. To remove, damage or worst of all destroy a soul is to serve the Sixth Watchtower, the tower of monsters and the Abyssal reflection of Awakening. Any who do so must be hunted down and destroyed. This does not preclude research into the soul for the purposes of defence, healing or strengthening, but this must never be at the detriment of another\u2019s. Some Tremere see the undead, shapechangers or other once-human creatures as being victims of soul afflictions and seek to cure them, whether they\u2019re asked to or not, though hardliners see more worth in cauterising the spread of these curses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b>Seek the Seventh Watchtower</b></b></span><br /> <br /> The five paths are like pure white light refracted from a prism, each one aspect of Truth, with the Watchtowers the first revelation a Mage achieves. The Seventh Watchtower, in Tremere philosophy, is the pure expression of Truth, the Platonic form which each Path derives from, offering Ascension to those who conquer it. The life of a Tremere should be the following of this Seventh Path, fighting towards greater truths as they fought to Awaken from the Lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b>Origins</b></b></span><br /> <br /> The Tremere order has a long shadow over its history. Regarded first as monster hunters and soul researchers by the others of the Diamond, in the 12th century the Order was revealed to be headed by foul soul stealers, who had devoured other Nameless Orders and Legacies in their pursuit of dominion over the soul and magic. Luckily, the influx of new recruits, most willful and iconoclast, granted by admission into the Diamond led to a cracking of their secrecy. Information and lore began to leak quicker than could be contained, the final blow being the dissemination of an unredacted copy of The Suspire to the other Orders.<br /> <br /> After the purge of the House masters, the question remained of what to do with remaining members who were judged to not have taken part in the leaders\u2019 excesses. Ultimately a cabal of seven Tremere mages, the very same who had leaked The Suspire to the rest of the Diamond, volunteered to be executed as symbols of the Order\u2019s past, to allow its rebirth. These were the Seven Martyrs and the Pure Suspire they wrote formed the basis of the redeemed order.<br /> <br /> In modern times the Order is treated by some with suspicion, though this is mediated somewhat by the Tremere\u2019s openness about their dark origins and their continued reputation as monster hunters. In fact, their transparency (at least compared to the rest of the Diamond) has lent them an expectation for more \u201cLeft-Handedness\u201d with the other Diamond Orders. While this is by no means a licence to commit crimes against Wisdom, often a Consilia will be more lenient with a Tremere member\u2019s choice of Mysteries than they would others, if only with the expectation that they will confirm why such topics are better left alone. The Order is legendary on how brutally they will come down on members discovered to be falling into the same corruption as their old masters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b>Mysteries</b></b></span><br /> <br /> The Tremere seek Mysteries that actively resist comprehension, are protected by powerful guardians or involve Supernal entities. Second only to the Mysterium, Strugglers are avid explorers of the ruins of the Time Before, Supernal Verges and stranger realms still, though they\u2019re less concerned with preservation than defeating their guardians and taking their treasures home. Tremere also often aggressively targets Seers and the Left-handed, driving them away from Mysteries and stealing their Artefacts for their own study. The more well defended it is, the more it must be worth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b>Magical Symbolism: Hunger</b></b></span><br /> <br /> The Tremere are never satisfied, their passion never waning, always seeking worthy challenges. They believe that Truth resides inside the precious soul and all answers can be found within. The Order\u2019s magical tools often incorporate hair, nails, spit or even blood and bone. These grossly physical implements ground the spiritual in the passion of the mortal. Maps, blueprints and records also feature, to better plan for the next challenge, or bugles, banners and even loud declarations to clearly state the intention of the Mage. When it comes to weapons, they range between obvious enough to display utter confidence, or concealed to surprise an unwary foe.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the Diamond\u2019s draconic symbolism, the Tremere embodies the Sanguis Draconis, the Blood of the Dragon: the motive force and ambition that drives the Awakened city and its people forward, purging stagnation and cleansing corruption. Blood must flow, or the beast will die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b>Hubris</b></b></span><br /> <br /> Tremere philosophy is predisposed to biting off more than it can chew and seems built to encourage Hubris in its adherents. The Order encourages seeking challenges, but bystanders can be caught up in the consequences. Raiding a Seer\u2019s Sanctum sparks reprisals, defeating a powerful spirit creates a vacuum in the Shadow and harrassing vampires or werewolves is a surefire way to get someone killed. Tremere fall when they forget the reason they are struggling is so that those following will not have to do so. But a saviour or martyr complex can just as easily lead a Tremere to ruin. Some Mysteries are too corrosive or demand utter immorality for the Wise to understand them safely, but Tremere can convince themselves that if they could master it, they could reverse the ill effects and return, triumphant, only to become another victim or a vector for the pain it spreads.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b>Concepts</b></b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Disciple of Jacob:</b> I know the creature I\u2019m following isn\u2019t human, despite the form it wears. When it thought it was alone, or only viewed by the faithful, it revealed its truth, the secret body of wires, circuits and stained glass. It can perform what the cult calls miracles, but only in service of the occult geometry it\u2019s trying to twist the new highway into. I can think of better uses for them. I\u2019ll have to rely on my magic in the end, but the classes in Judo, Sambo, Sumo and MMA are the foundations of my victory.<br /> <br /> <b>Unioniser:</b> I must have worked at six to eight different warehouses in the last year alone. I\u2019m in good with lady luck and always have experience needed somewhere else. Management\u2019s getting antsy, but with a quick tug of probability they\u2019re never around when my co-workers are reading the leaflets I\u2019ve given out. The spirits of conformity the Seer flunky sent turn tail and run when they see me. With one strike, we\u2019ll topple the pylon. Next, the whole damn pyramid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Stereotypes</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Adamantium Arrow:</b> Service is mastery is just a fancy way of denying your own autonomy. A righteous battle is still righteous, even if nobody asked you to fight it.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians:</b> We have to give them credit for taking the fight to the Thrones and our predecessors. But we admit to our mistakes.<br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium:</b> They claim to oppose Pancryptia, yet keep the lore to themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Ladder:</b> We\u2019re here to keep you honest.<br /> <br /> <b>Free Council:</b> The enemy isn\u2019t hiding in plain sight, little cousins.<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne: </b>Your thrones are first.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27946-keyboard-cowboy","user":"Keyboard Cowboy","date":".  Added link to Tremere post 04-24-2023, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27946-keyboard-cowboy","name":"Keyboard Cowboy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:59:26-07:00","id":1509498,"title":"","content":"&quot;your Thrones are first&quot; is a raw fucking like. Congratulations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:28:31-07:00","id":1509502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1509498#post1509498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;your Thrones are first&quot; is a raw fucking like. Congratulations!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27946-keyboard-cowboy","name":"Keyboard Cowboy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T15:04:09-07:00","id":1509525,"title":"","content":"It's well put together, with some clever ideas, such as the Tremere being super-open to combat their reputation. However, it honestly makes me think the remaining Tremere would, if not simply dissolved into, have become a faction of, the Silver Ladder. Hell, maybe even a legacy within the Ladder. The similarities are just a bit too strong in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T16:36:58-07:00","id":1509533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1509525#post1509525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's well put together, with some clever ideas, such as the Tremere being super-open to combat their reputation. However, it honestly makes me think the remaining Tremere would, if not simply dissolved into, have become a faction of, the Silver Ladder. Hell, maybe even a legacy within the Ladder. The similarities are just a bit too strong in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in a suitable alternative modern setting, it could work a lot like how there was once simultaneously Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates, a similar overall thesis but with marked distinctions in methodology, rites, and priorities. I'd think a Silver Ladder in such circumstances would place a much stronger focus on the concept of perfected hierarchy that is their name, the Mysteries of how Imperium is attained by building the ladder and providing the guidance on how to climb it, rather than battling monsters and pursuing more active personifications of hierarchy. I also feel as though this rendering of the Tremere isn't exactly instructive towards Sleepers, even if they think it's valuable to not be totally alienated from them.<br /> <br /> And if there's tension and competition between the Ladder's position of being the diplomatic and legalistic force that holds five Orders across two sects as a society and the Tremere regarding themselves as being a driving, motivating force in the Pentacle by unsettling the others, I think that could be leaned into as a source of compelling conflict.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there should be anything in this schema to address the notion in Tremere lore that the Seventh Dragon provided a means to heal the affliction in their souls that came from imprisoned monsters turning the tables on them. I think that to get free of that and then lose any element of being compromised if outsiders just purge the Order of Reapers would be a bit too clean.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Dragons, I think it might be worth addressing Tremere notions of the Sixth Dragon, that the existence of several forms of monster like vampires profanes the human soul in its own right. Even the canon modern Tremere regard opposition to such entities to be of great significance. I think that's the sort of thing that either gets referenced more directly or has an additional history point on why they might have shifted away from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T07:02:00-07:00","id":1509714,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Very cool. I definitely wanna use this. Only things that are missing are Order Rote specialties. I'm guessing Intimidate(reflecting general attitude) and Occult(they def have a focus on understanding monsters and such) would be on that list, but not sure what the third would be. Survival isn't bad(they share the mysterium's penchant for exploration), but Weaponry seems good too(kicking ass seems like part of their thing). I'll bet there a bunch of good possibilities.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Empathy, Occult, and Subterfuge</span>\u200b are the Order Rote skills for Tremere in Nameless and Accursed, but I don't think it matches this reborn version of the Tremere. At minimum, Subterfuge is probably gonna have been changed based on my read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24407-radriel7","name":"Radriel7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24407_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T06:12:35-07:00","id":1510347,"title":"","content":"Legacies for the Order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T00:45:05-07:00","id":1510687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix853457</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1510347#post1510347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies for the Order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Al.ost all left handed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T15:07:02-07:00","id":1510722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1509525#post1509525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's well put together, with some clever ideas, such as the Tremere being super-open to combat their reputation. However, it honestly makes me think the remaining Tremere would, if not simply dissolved into, have become a faction of, the Silver Ladder. Hell, maybe even a legacy within the Ladder. The similarities are just a bit too strong in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast, I've been sitting here wondering why there's a need for revision at all from the medieval forward-face order of the Tremere-Cut out the Suspire and the rest is pretty operable.<br /> <br /> While the Tremere and the Silver Ladder agree on the worth of ambition, the difference is to what end they work it towards.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder are primarily interested in perfecting society-put the true king on the true king's throne, and the true tailor in their clothing store and the true farmer in their field, and the world will submit itself to humanity, and tyrants will have no purchase upon the diamond kingdom. The Silver Ladder believe that if a wizard is to be a wizard, in an ideal world there would be no obstacle to that, that Awakening would just be given to the deserving. Their paternal interests lie in then constructing their diamond-they're the ones interested in cooperation, coordination, and assigning everyone to where they will do best.<br /> <br /> The Tremere, by contrast (based on what we have for the medieval form so far), have no interest in sociological concerns. THey're concerned with the individuals and with the world, and that buffer between that we call society will just sort itself out-it doesn't matter if a &quot;true king&quot; is on the throne, the world will submit itself when you tame the land, slay or corral the beasts, and otherwise <i>make it submit</i>. If a wizard is to be a wizard, they'll take the light of the Watchtowers as a rope and <i>bring it to heel</i>. If a person is truly to be a king, then they must be willing to claim the kingdom and <i>make it an extension of their will</i>. And mind you, that's assuming kings are desirable at all-their missives bring them against gods and monsters, but rulers do just as much to wield power they don't deserve and keep it from others. This is why the Tremere markedly aren't systematically Seers.<br /> <br /> The order on the whole leans more libertarian*, even objectivist (as much as those terms can apply to a medieval organization), being more concerned with making wholeness in the self and destroying nexuses of stagnancy for the flow of power. Their individual ambition is to seize what is theirs, and if nothing can be seized from them, then that's where they're supposed to be <i>for now</i>. If they make a perfect society in their practice, it's because they have made a consumate whole soul, starting with themselves and then making whole the soul of humanity, and then the world. They have more in common with the Adamantine Arrow and Guardians of the Veil than the Silver Ladder, but prioritize the world against enemies as their targets, and believe the way to fight the Abyss is not treat magic as frail, but as something to keep a firm grasp on.<br /> <br /> THe SIlver Ladder believes Magic is Humanity's Birthright, and things will be right when everyone take's their accordant place on the Silver Ladder. The Tremere believe Magic must be Tamed, and things will be right when all of magic no longer bucks against those who would grasp it.<br /> <br /> *as it's usually meant, not how Americans use the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-04-2023, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T02:38:38-07:00","id":1510764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1510722#post1510722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast, I've been sitting here wondering why there's a need for revision at all from the medieval forward-face order of the Tremere-Cut out the Suspire and the rest is pretty operable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do it however you want. Hell, keep them as a Diamond Order with Hollows at the top, that could be fun (I actually don't know if that'd even work). But I think it's not unreasonable to expect a purged Tremere to feel that they need to show extra contrition before the rest of the Diamond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THe SIlver Ladder believes Magic is Humanity's Birthright, and things will be right when everyone take's their accordant place on the Silver Ladder. The Tremere believe Magic must be Tamed, and things will be right when all of magic no longer bucks against those who would grasp it. </div> </div> </div>To me that doesn't seem different enough. Also, I don't think that's how the Cryptopoly works. You don't need to take your place in it, it's a way of categorising people where they already are. I dunno, maybe that'll change when TotP turns up.<br /> <br /> I do take your point that their activities are quite different to the regular Ladder. Though, it's not like the Ladder doesn't have specialist groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T06:24:29-07:00","id":1510775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1510764#post1510764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me that doesn't seem different enough. Also, I don't think that's how the Cryptopoly works. You don't need to take your place in it, it's a way of categorising people where they already are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see two ways to elaborate on the Order being motivated to have people take their place on the Silver Ladder of Being.<br /> <br /> One is to help people find the occupation that is most suited to and fulfilling towards them. Help the artists stuck in day jobs fulfil their art, help the lawyers who'd be more happy making and selling pretzels to find the confidence to not get hung up on the sunk costs of law school, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The other is to actually arrange roles that exist into the hierarchy that the Order think facilitates the creation of Hieraconis and the assumption of Imperium. As it is, there are a lot of existing power distributions that are not the way the Ladder thinks things ought to be; scientists who must defer to politicians and the like, when as I recall they say it should be the other way around.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T09:18:34-07:00","id":1510797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1510775#post1510775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see two ways to elaborate on the Order being motivated to have people take their place on the Silver Ladder of Being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it simply changed between editions. Like, rereading the SL entry in the 2e core... is subtly different to the way things are discussed in their book.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the tenet of the Star in the SL book is about the right of the Ladder to run Mage society, it doesn't mention sleepers. In the 2e core, it's about defining a path to enlightenment for the sleepers, including a ladder metaphor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other is to actually arrange roles that exist into the hierarchy that the Order think facilitates the creation of Hieraconis and the assumption of Imperium. As it is, there are a lot of existing power distributions that are not the way the Ladder thinks things ought to be; scientists who must defer to politicians and the like, when as I recall they say it should be the other way around. </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Though at least in the 1e, the idea was that this was a real hierarchy. The Hiereoi and Technoi are where they are because they define the world that Polemarchs exist in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T11:14:53-07:00","id":1510894,"title":"","content":"I find myself thinking that these are fine distinctions that would make sense as topics of debate for within the Silver Ladder itself in a manner that would further distinguish it from the Tremere when I see no indication that they're concerned by such a topic whatsoever. Ultimately the only commonality I'm seeing between them is a concept of Imperium, but the ideas of who that is for and what it entails to acquire it appear to be drastically different. That can ultimately mark them as members of the same sect who are using common terminology while still functioning as separate Orders if they manage to have a different central thesis and social position.<br /> <br /> Although that should also consider the extent to which Second Edition places greater emphasis on the Diamond Orders as things with more organic histories, traceable origin points and messy evolutions with a capacity to cross-pollinate and where the idea of modelling themselves on inheritors of some wizard caste system is largely a template they impose on themselves that still has some spillage at the edges.<br /> <br /> I should think this is most evident in the idea that the Keepers of the Word and the Pancryptiates were separate Orders for longer than they have been the Mysterium, even with the most conservative models for when the Diamond really comes into existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T09:53:34-07:00","id":1511548,"title":"","content":"Legacies for the <b>Redeemed Tremere? </b><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T11:15:15-07:00","id":1511552,"title":"","content":"It could be neat to have redeemed Tremere maintain their tradition of subverting hostile Legacies. They would have to be careful to avoid becoming <i>Scelesti</i> or <i>Reapers</i>, but many <i>Seers of the Throne</i> hold Legacies that are neutral in their symbolism, or at least could be reinterpreted to be so. Imagine Tremere finding out about <i>Princes of Many Masks</i> or <i>Architects of the Future</i> and becoming dead set on rooting them out, kicking their assess, stealing all their resources, adapting their Legacies to be Pentacle (Hexacle? It looks too much like a Star of David. Honeycomb?) compliant and sharing them with all who ask.<br /> <br /> There are also plenty of Legacies that Seers share with other Mages, and they can be a target, with Tremere trying to give their allies monopoly. Imagine Tremere <i>Stone Scribes</i> planning to kill their counterparts from the Pyramind, and then writing down their Final Names, as is proper. The more peaceful Legacy members are grateful for reclaimed lore and are trying not to ask questions they don't want to know the answers to.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there are Legacies mean to interact with the wider supernatural. Both <i>Bokor</i> and <i>Bene Ashmedai</i> have selfish motives counterbalanced by their sense of duty, which is what &quot;good&quot; Tremere aspire to be. Such Tremere could effectively Banishers, while officially avoiding that label.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T01:32:11-07:00","id":1511591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1509497-redeemed-tremere-what-if-the-tremere-had-remained-in-the-pentacle?p=1511552#post1511552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be neat to have redeemed Tremere maintain their tradition of subverting hostile Legacies. They would have to be careful to avoid becoming <i>Scelesti</i> or <i>Reapers</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's perfectly possible to be an opponent to certain Legacies without needing to harness Paradox or steal souls. For that matter, there are plenty of outright Left-Handed Legacies that are neither Scelesti or Reapers themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such Tremere could effectively Banishers, while officially avoiding that label.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that would make somebody a Banisher any more than the Free Council having a creed of &quot;Destroy the Followers of the Lie&quot; does. You're not a Banisher if you violently pursue other mages due to incompatible ideology or practices, only if it's primarily because they're a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T14:33:39-07:00","id":1532869,"title":"","content":"All 8 Diamond\u2019s Order draconic symbolism including stuff from Tome of the Pentacle<br /> <br /> Symbolism from the core book<br /> Admantine Arrow:Ungula Draconis;The Talon of the Dragon<br /> Guardians of the Veil:Visus Draconis;The Eye of the Dragon<br /> Mysterium:Alae Draconis;The Wings of the Dragon<br /> Silver Ladder:Vox Draconis; The Voice of the Dragon<br /> <br /> Symbolism form Tome of the Pentacle<br /> Keeper of the Word:Corpus Draconis;Body of the Dragon<br /> Pancryptiates:Thesaurus Draconis;The Hoard the Dragon<br /> Tremere:Fames Draconis; The Hunger of the Dragon<br /> Free Council: Amira Draconis; The Soul of the Dragon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}